cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this workflow in your research, please cite the Zenodo release (once available)
  and the associated manuscript (once available).
title: Heliocot: A segmentation-to-PLA workflow for diurnal cotton canopy orientation dynamics
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Çakaloğulları
    given-names: Uğur
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4175-1815
  - family-names: İştipliler
    given-names: Deniz
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0887-1121
abstract: >-
  Heliocot is an open, reproducible segmentation-to-PLA workflow for top-down field RGB images of cotton.
  It converts instance segmentation masks into reference-area standardized projected leaf area (PLA) time series
  and supports quantifying diurnal canopy orientation dynamics.
keywords:
  - cotton
  - field phenotyping
  - instance segmentation
  - projected leaf area
  - diurnal dynamics
  - canopy orientation
license: MIT
